    "narrative": "The Austin Waves enter today\u2019s slate with a heavy focus on high-upside speed threats as we navigate the scarcity of the SB category. **Heliot Ramos** currently headlines our daily projections, anchoring the outfield with a score of 88.2, fueled by a favorable matchup against a starter with a ballooning 5.12 xERA. His presence at the top of the order creates a vital runway for **Jackson Merrill**, who boasts a 81.4 efficiency score; the combination of a hitter-friendly venue and wind conditions blowing out toward right-center field provides the structural support needed for a high-ceiling performance. Conversely, **Jorge Polanco** remains a marginal start at 53.8; despite an favorable wind advantage, the matchup against Nola presents significant regression risk for his batting average, making him a volatile play in our middle infield.\n\nThe most difficult decision on the bench involved **Jordan Westburg**, who narrowly missed the starting cut with a score of 59.2. While his raw power profile is enticing, we opted to favor the platoon-advantaged speed profiles of **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** and **Nasim Nunez**, whose sprint-speed metrics are essential for our 5x5 objectives. **Jacob Wilson** and **Brayan Rocchio** were also considered but ultimately benched to preserve our limited remaining game caps for higher-leverage matchups later this week. We are closely monitoring the status of **Luis Robert Jr.**, who remains sidelined on the IL, leaving a noticeable hole in our stolen base potential. With **Kyle Tucker**, **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.**, and **Gunnar Henderson** all enjoying an off-day, the rest of the roster\u2014including **Andy Pages**, **Drake Baldwin**, and **Cole Carrigg**\u2014must maximize their efficiency today to maintain our standing. We are keeping a close watch on potential weather delays for the **Josh Jung** and **Coby Mayo** contest, as any postponement would force a rotation shift into our bench depth of **Miguel Vargas**, **Curtis Mead**, **Sam Antonacci**, **Dominic Smith**, **Wade Meckler**, **Liam Hicks**, **Luis Lara**, and **Denzer Guzman**.",
